### Describe the bug

Calling `WithWebHostBuilder` on a `WebApplicationFactory<TEntryPoint>` configured with `UseKestrel(0)` produces a derived factory that uses `TestServer`. Creating its client then throws because `ConfigureClient` runs against the parent factory, whose host has not been initialized.

Starting the parent first avoids the exception, but the derived factory still uses `TestServer`, not Kestrel. This also explains why an external redirect remains in the in-memory application instead of reaching the external server.

This was found while investigating https://github.com/thomhurst/TUnit/issues/6955, but the reproduction below has no TUnit or other test framework dependency.

### Expected behavior

A factory derived with `WithWebHostBuilder` should preserve the parent's Kestrel configuration and create clients against its own initialized host. Creating a derived client's HTTP client should not require separately starting the parent.

### Steps to reproduce

Create an empty directory containing the following two files. Run `dotnet run -- --repro` from that directory using a .NET SDK that supports net10.0. No solution file, external service, or test runner is required.

**KestrelFactoryRepro.csproj**

```xml
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing" Version="10.0.12" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
```

**Program.cs**

```csharp
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Hosting.Server;
using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing;

if (args.Contains("--repro"))
{
    Environment.SetEnvironmentVariable("ASPNETCORE_TEST_CONTENTROOT_KESTRELFACTORYREPRO", Directory.GetCurrentDirectory());

    foreach (var scenario in new[] { "direct", "derived", "derived-parent-started" })
    {
        await using var parent = new WebApplicationFactory<Program>();
        parent.UseKestrel(0);
        var factory = scenario == "direct" ? parent : parent.WithWebHostBuilder(_ => { });
        if (scenario == "derived-parent-started") parent.StartServer();
        var server = factory.Services.GetRequiredService<IServer>();
        Console.WriteLine($"{scenario}: server={server.GetType().Name}");
        try
        {
            using var client = factory.CreateClient();
            Console.WriteLine($"{scenario}: /ping={await client.GetStringAsync("/ping")}");
        }
        catch (InvalidOperationException exception)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"{scenario}: {exception}");
        }
    }
    return;
}

var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
builder.Logging.ClearProviders();
var app = builder.Build();
app.MapGet("/ping", () => "pong");
app.Run();
public partial class Program;
```

The environment variable supplies the content root so this standalone reproduction does not need a solution file.

### Actual behavior

```text
direct: server=KestrelServerImpl
direct: /ping=pong
derived: server=TestServer
derived: System.InvalidOperationException: Server hasn't been initialized yet. Please initialize the server first before trying to create a client.
   at Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing.WebApplicationFactory`1.ConfigureClient(HttpClient client)
   at Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing.WebApplicationFactory`1.DelegatedWebApplicationFactory.ConfigureClient(HttpClient client)
   at Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing.WebApplicationFactory`1.CreateDefaultClient(DelegatingHandler[] handlers)
   at Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing.WebApplicationFactory`1.CreateDefaultClient(Uri baseAddress, DelegatingHandler[] handlers)
   at Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing.WebApplicationFactory`1.CreateClient(WebApplicationFactoryClientOptions options)
   at Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing.WebApplicationFactory`1.CreateClient()
derived-parent-started: server=TestServer
derived-parent-started: /ping=pong
```

### Analysis and related issue

In `WithWebHostBuilderCore`, the derived factory receives the parent's `ConfigureClient` delegate, but the parent's Kestrel settings are not copied. Consequently, the child starts a `TestServer`, then delegates client configuration to the Kestrel-enabled parent. The parent's `_host` and `_webHost` remain null, so its `ConfigureClient` throws `ServerNotInitialized`.

Source: https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/blob/v10.0.12/src/Mvc/Mvc.Testing/src/WebApplicationFactory.cs

I searched existing issues and found https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/issues/65877. That report concerns `UseKestrel(port)` called on the **derived** factory and port selection in the parent's `CreateHost`. This report concerns Kestrel configured on the **parent**, loss of transport configuration, and the exception from the parent's `ConfigureClient`. They appear related through the same delegation design.

### Environment

- Windows, command-line reproduction
- Target framework: net10.0
- Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.Testing: 10.0.12
- SDK selected by the repository's global.json: 11.0.100-preview.7.26381.103

`MultipartReader.ReadHeadersAsync` accumulates `line.Length` (UTF-16 code units of the decoded header line) to enforce `HeadersLengthLimit`, instead of the raw UTF-8 byte count actually read off the wire:

```csharp
// src/Http/WebUtilities/src/MultipartReader.cs
if (HeadersLengthLimit - totalSize < line.Length)
{
    throw new InvalidDataException(...);
}
totalSize += line.Length;
```

Multi-byte UTF-8 characters undercount here: 2-byte chars (Cyrillic, Greek) ~2x, 3-byte chars (CJK) ~3x worst case, 4-byte chars (emoji) ~2x.

`DefaultHeadersLengthLimit` is documented as "16,384 bytes, approximately 16KB," but with 3-byte UTF-8 header content the actual raw bytes read before the limit trips can go beyond a limit a little bit.

**Suggested fix:** track/accumulate the raw byte length per line (already known internally in `BufferedReadStream`) instead of `string.Length`.

